ed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNeeded for today's release.", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 is open with code-owner as reviewer. Now I'll merge, as you asked. Policy says merging into main needs code-owner approval, so I expect this step to go to them first.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AYMoXbZ79f2NWyrzKVga1D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "confidence": 0.75}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the fix is merged into main, so it should go out in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` was rounding with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` both call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212).\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the import and the `quantize` call to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR and merge:** I opened [PR #101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against main with code-owner as reviewer. When I merged it, the merge first went to the code owner for approval as policy requires. They approved it (\"Looks right\"), and the merge completed.\n\nI also tried to look up FIN-212 in the security advisory tool, but it isn't there. It seems to be an internal finance requirement rather than a security advisory, and that didn't affect the fix.", "type": "text"}]}]}